/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/H3Cit-formation.dat -- the neutral citric acid as the sum of its fully dissociated form:
      Cit(3-) + 3 H+  <=>  H3Cit

  logK25 and dH are the selected values of Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231, Table 7.22 (Citrate), p. 265 (evaluation grades AAB / AAB / AAB,
  scale: standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K, I = 0):
      pK1 = 3.128, pK2 = 4.761, pK3 = 6.396
      dH1 = 4.07 kJ/mol, dH2 = 2.23 kJ/mol, dH3 = -3.38 kJ/mol
  This record carries the sum of those steps (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The enthalpy is the EVALUATED dH_ion of the same table as the pK, not a difference of formation
  enthalpies: the two kinds of number are kept apart and cross-checked in
  docs/design/organic-acids-in-the-catalogue.md.  Hand-curated organic chemistry, not PHREEQC.

  The inverse of the records written from the neutral master; a case declares one master and
  the closure activates the record reachable from it.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species H3Cit; masters ( { ion Cit; nu 1; } { ion H; nu 3; } );
      logK25 14.285; dH -2920; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231, Table 7.22 (Citrate), p. 265: pK1 = 3.128, pK2 = 4.761, pK3 = 6.396; dH1 = 4.07 kJ/mol, dH2 = 2.23 kJ/mol, dH3 = -3.38 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K, I = 0)";
